  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">1. Operating Scope &amp; Legal Framework</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      Spice and Sail Zanzibar is a locally owned tour operator and private transfer specialist based in Mbuzini, Mjini Magharibi, Zanzibar, Tanzania. We operate in compliance with the Zanzibar Tourism Act No. 6 of 2009. While our formal Zanzibar Commission for Tourism (ZCT) operator licence application is in process, all field excursions, private transfers, and ocean charters are fulfilled in partnership with fully certified, Zanzibari-licensed guides, vessel captains, and authorized transport providers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">2. Transparent Pricing &amp; Inclusions</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      Rates published on our website and generated by our interactive fare engines are verified catalogue planning ranges. Every booking quote provided by our reservations team is fixed and inclusive of all mandatory government taxes, guide fees, and official marine conservation levies (such as Menai Bay Marine Reserve $10 and Mnemba Marine Reserve $25). Optional personal expenses (such as museum admissions or discretionary gratuities) are explicitly itemized prior to confirmation.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">3. Booking Enquiries, Deposits &amp; Confirmation Process</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      To provide maximum flexibility and financial security for our guests and local operations, Spice &amp; Sail operates on a tiered deposit framework:
    </p>
    <ul style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75; margin-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      <li><strong>Private Airport &amp; Inter-Hotel Transfers:</strong> <strong>Zero advance deposit</strong>. Reserve without prepayment and pay your private driver directly upon meeting him at the airport or hotel lobby (cash USD/TZS or driver mobile card machine).</li>
      <li><strong>Marine Tours &amp; Boat Charters (Safari Blue, Mnemba Atoll, Prison Island + Nakupenda Sandbank, Dolphin Tours, Sunset Dhows, Catamaran Charters):</strong> <strong>20% advance deposit</strong> required upon booking via a secure DPO or Pesapal payment link sent to you on WhatsApp. This deposit locks your dedicated boat captain, crew, fuel, and fresh morning seafood market procurement. The remaining 80% balance is settled upon boarding on the day of your tour.</li>
      <li><strong>Fly-in Bush Safaris (Serengeti, Nyerere, Ruaha):</strong> <strong>30% advance deposit</strong> required upon booking to issue non-refundable scheduled domestic airline tickets and TANAPA national park permits.</li>
    </ul>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      When you submit a booking request through our website or concierge, you receive an <strong>Enquiry Reference (#SP-YYYY-XXXXXX)</strong> confirming that your request is safely logged in our system. Our operations team then verifies live availability and connects with you directly on WhatsApp to issue your confirmed itinerary and secure payment link.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">4. Payment Methods &amp; Cancellation Policy</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      <strong>Payment Methods:</strong> We accept online card payments (Visa, Mastercard, American Express via 3D-Secure payment links powered by DPO Group and Pesapal) sent to you on WhatsApp, local mobile money (M-Pesa, Airtel Money, Tigo Pesa), and cash (clean United States Dollars USD printed post-2013 per East African banking standards, or Tanzanian Shillings TZS at prevailing market rates).
    </p>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      <strong>Important:</strong> We do not collect card details on this website. After your booking is confirmed, our team sends the DPO or Pesapal payment link directly to you on WhatsApp.
    </p>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      <strong>Fair Cancellation &amp; Weather Guarantee:</strong>
    </p>
    <ul style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75; margin-left: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      <li><strong>Transfers &amp; Walking Tours:</strong> Free cancellation up to 12 hours before pickup.</li>
      <li><strong>Sea Tours &amp; Boat Charters:</strong> Free cancellation up to <strong>24 hours before tour departure</strong> for a 100% full refund of your deposit. Because fresh seafood is purchased at 5:30 AM and boat captains are pre-paid, cancellations within 24 hours forfeit the 20% deposit to cover these non-recoverable partner costs.</li>
      <li><strong>Captain's Weather Guarantee:</strong> In the event of rough sea conditions, heavy swells, or maritime weather warnings issued by the Zanzibar Maritime Authority making sea crossings unsafe, we offer an immediate <strong>100% full refund</strong> or priority rescheduling at zero extra charge.</li>
      <li><strong>Fly-in Safaris:</strong> Governed by scheduled domestic airline ticket cancellation rules and TANAPA park authority regulations.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">5. Safety, Marine Equipment &amp; Passenger Welfare</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      All vessels utilized for ocean activities carry marine safety gear, certified life jackets for adults and children, first-aid kits, and communication devices. All private road vehicles are licensed passenger minivans with functioning air-conditioning and seatbelts. Guests are required to follow all safety briefings from guides and vessel captains.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">6. Cultural Respect &amp; Wildlife Ethics</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      Zanzibar is a culturally rich, predominantly Muslim society. Guests are requested to dress modestly (covering shoulders and knees) when walking through Stone Town, rural villages, and local markets. In wildlife and marine environments, we enforce strict ethical rules: zero dolphin chasing, zero touching of corals or marine turtles, and mandatory safe approach distances.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.4rem; color: #003853; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">7. Statutory Insurance &amp; Liability</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--dct-text-muted); line-height: 1.75;">
      All international travelers visiting Zanzibar are required by the Revolutionary Government of Zanzibar to hold official Zanzibar Inbound Travel Insurance issued by the Zanzibar Insurance Corporation (ZIC, $44/adult). Our operations carry public passenger liability coverage. We strongly advise travelers to hold comprehensive medical and travel cancellation insurance.
    </p>
  </section>

